# 13 hiking club
(f"Please write a short message for the Summit Seekers Hiking Club about our winter walk on Sunday 18 January. We're climbing Lugnaquilla, meeting at the Glenmalure car park at 9am. The walk is about 16 km and takes six hours. Hikers need winter boots, gloves and a flask. The leader is Brian Kehoe. {C}",
 ["Lugnaquilla", "Glenmalure car park", "16 km", "Brian Kehoe"],
 [("Can you write a hiking club message about how car sharing will work this season? Prose, please, no bullets.",
   "This season we want to make car sharing the normal way of getting to walks. Here is how it will work:\n\n- Drivers post the number of free seats in the group by Thursday.\n- Passengers reply to claim a seat.\n- Passengers give the driver €5 towards fuel.\n\nSharing cars cuts the cost of each walk and reduces the pressure on small car parks at the trailheads.",
   "This season we want to make car sharing the normal way of getting to walks. Drivers will post the number of free seats in the group by Thursday, and passengers can reply to claim a seat. Each passenger then gives the driver €5 towards fuel. Sharing cars cuts the cost of each walk and reduces the pressure on small car parks at the trailheads."),
  ("Please write a message to the hiking club about the safety rules on walks. Please write it as prose, without a list.",
   "With the darker months coming, here is a reminder of the club's safety rules for every walk:\n\n- Stay between the leader and the back marker at all times.\n- Tell the leader if you need to stop or turn back.\n- Carry a fully charged phone and a whistle.\n\nThe leaders may change or shorten a route if the weather turns. Their decision is final, and it is always made with the group's safety in mind.",
   "With the darker months coming, here is a reminder of the club's safety rules for every walk. Please stay between the leader and the back marker at all times, and tell the leader if you need to stop or turn back. Everyone should carry a fully charged phone and a whistle. The leaders may change or shorten a route if the weather turns. Their decision is final, and it is always made with the group's safety in mind.")]),
